  "last_message": "I added a new page, `docs/features/pickup-reminders.md`, explaining why pickup reminders go by SMS, and listed it in `docs/features/README.md`. It's a feature page rather than a decision record because the docs map only allows records for decisions that are hard to undo and affect more than one module. The reminder channel fails both tests: it's one setting, `CHANNEL` in `larder/reminders.py`, and it was switched back from email to SMS in one step.\n\nThe page tells the story from issue 52, so it doesn't depend on the issue tracker staying around:\n- **The cost:** SMS costs about 40 euros a month and email is free, and people keep asking to switch. Issue 52 was the third request within the year.\n- **The email trial:** reminders went by email from April to June 2025. The email provider's report showed 34% of reminder emails were never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup is a packed bag whose fresh food is thrown away at closing time.\n- **Why email doesn't reach people:** many members share one phone in the family and never check email, but they see an SMS.\n- **The outcome:** reminders went back to SMS on July 1, 2025, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August. The maintainer kept SMS and closed the issue.\n\nEverything on the page comes from `notes/issue-52.md` and `larder/reminders.py`. I didn't add any rule for judging future proposals, because the repository doesn't state one. I haven't committed the change.",
